  "id": "mini-mental-state-examination",
  "term": "Mini-Mental State Examination",
  "definition": "The Mini-Mental State Examination is a widely used cognitive screening test for people with neurological or psychiatric disorders. In ALS, it is used to screen cognitive functioning, but because it is not adjusted for motor impairment it may be less suitable than ALS-specific tools for detecting milder early cognitive problems.",
